From: Pingouin
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: Pingouin's boot splash, the icon's stripes and penguin

What: the boot splash of pingouin-cocoa-boot-splash.patch shows the app
icon's six rainbow stripes over the whole window, top to bottom, with the
penguin in the middle (0.42 of the height), instead of Omarchy's logo; it
is still (no start animation). It is on by default again
(PINGOUIN_BOOT_SPLASH=0 turns it off). The rest is upstream's: it holds over
the firmware, GRUB and Linux's console until the desktop is lit, then fades;
black once the desktop turned an output off; the slow-start hint, now white,
under the penguin.
How: pingouin_splash_pixels draws the splash with Core Graphics at the
output's size in pixels; the GL layers and the IOSurface path blit it as a
texture made at that size, the overlay layer shows the same bytes tagged
with the window's colour space (GL's pixels show unconverted). The penguin
is a PNG in ui/pingouin-splash-art.h (runtime/tools/make-splash-art.sh).
Upstream: Pingouin only (branding).
